{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/716811-garou-attitudes-towards-holidays","id":716811,"title":"Garou attitudes towards holidays.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-22T19:07:54-07:00","id":716811,"title":"Garou attitudes towards holidays.","content":"With halloween getting close... am wondering How do you think the Garou especialy homids, or human kinfolk would view human holidays<br /> <br /> since they know that the world is animistic pretty clearly.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, its something to do with your family calls back to your own childhood etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T19:15:06-07:00","id":716840,"title":"","content":"Well I would imagine most homids would celebrate them because well they did before they changed. Plus the fianna always love an excuse for a party....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T23:01:21-07:00","id":717472,"title":"","content":"Fianna might perform rites and celebrate Samhain or Yule due to their ties to fairies- it may bear little resemblance to our festivities on Halloween or Christmas but it could still be fun to have the Garou do something on those days.<br /> <br /> I imagine western Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers do something for the holidays, as entrenched as they are in human culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T23:33:36-07:00","id":717590,"title":"","content":"Though GWs and BGs are more likely to engage in secular holidays rather than religious ones (or the secular aspects of religious ones that are highly mainstream).<br /> <br /> That said, most Tribes are linked pretty closely to real human cultures, and a lot of them place value in promoting the &quot;older&quot; or more &quot;traditional&quot; aspects of those cultures as they feel that promotes a better bias towards the Tribes' ideals. Uktena and Wendigo are likely to be very involved with the traditional religions of their kin as part of their preservationist streak; as an example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T15:37:18-07:00","id":720792,"title":"","content":"Many holidays have traditional or at least greater spiritual meaning, while I doubt Garou are going are going to care much about Mother's day(created by the greeting card industry!), there are many harvest and death festivals this time of year, there are many solstice festivals around christmas etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:53:05-07:00","id":721401,"title":"","content":"I too imagine a few of the younger homids might celebrate all the holidays if they could. Something fun and worth celebrating from their old lives that makes them feel better for a moment about facing the daunting tasks and possible death waiting for them.<br /> <br /> Whereas I imagine the older garou thinking &quot;great another freakin holiday. At this rate that chemical factory and warehouse of banes is never going to get sorted out. I give up. Pass me another bottle of liquid harano. You know in my day we saw the moot as christmas that we got time and time again. These kids though...geez...all they want to do is take every day off to celebrate something nothing to do with the litany or the Caern Totem. Are they still looking for recruits in the amazon? Maybe a tour their will put them to focus and appreciate what they have already...or thin out there numbers enough not to have a party every week...what?...I'm kidding...a little.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T11:08:44-07:00","id":723672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/716811-garou-attitudes-towards-holidays#post716811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">since they know that the world is animistic pretty clearly.</div> </div> </div> </div>They know that an animistic spirit world is real, but any Garou without blinders on also knows there are plenty of evidence that the Garou view is not solely correct. True Faith exists, and even though Garou probably run into it less often than vampires, they know that the power True Faith displays have to come somewhere. They also know a High Umbra exists, and that creatures resembling angels and demons are encountered there. They also know that various wizards, mystics, yogis, and witches sometimes try to claim their caerns, and that there powers are not always explainable by contact with spirits.<br /> <br /> The Garou have objective evidence their religion is based on something real. They also know that others have the same benefit. The Garou are very arrogant and likely dimissive of it, but anyone with an open mind realizes that there is either something about Tellurian they don't know, or that there is a lot more to the universe than just their view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T11:50:48-07:00","id":723834,"title":"","content":"oh another thing is the gift &quot;Bury the wolf&quot; appropiate for a holiday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T12:18:55-07:00","id":723920,"title":"","content":"A bunch of traditional christian dates subsume festivals and holy dates of pagan origins, so i would guess it's a case-by-case basis thing, depending on the tribe's specific cultural framework and varying even more among groups of tribes not associated with any one human culture/osciety in particular, as is the case with not only Glass Walkers &amp; Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, Stargazers, Shadow Lords &amp; Silver Fangs (western european pretensions notwithstanding). Red Talons obviously any and all such constructions that do not relate to what they can't track by the movement of stars on the sky or feel in the winds and woods around them. Solstices &amp; Equinoxes might be the closest times to universal holydays across all tribes, i would guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T18:52:59-07:00","id":724726,"title":"","content":"Considering that most Hollidays have ties with older things and older traditions, the Garou and the other shifters probably celebrate the ones that are closest to their culture and origins, with a whole bevy of Just Garou and Tribe hollidays. I've always seen a need for the Garou to let their steam out, so i believe there's a lot of partying going around whether to celebrate the spirits, mark great deeds, lament the fallen or just celebrate being alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T08:14:22-07:00","id":725990,"title":"","content":"I don't know I can see a lot of Garou not buying a great deal of the Garou's/Tribe's lore as gospel. I've also seen this as a bit of a weakness of WtA as a line, as it tries to push that various Tribes focused on certain people's, but also seems to ignore or avoid any concept that people might hold a modern faith dear and call BS on some of the stuff they are taught. I mean it really seems there would be, maybe not a lot, but some individuals that denied the concept of animistic totems and reflavored various spirits to be, (in a simplistic sense) angels or demons. Seemed like a particularly noticeable omission and lacking area that for the Tribes that put so much emphasis on cultural heritage, they forget that modern religions exist or where intrinsic to many of those cultures. Not the old pagan ones, (unless they are a neo-pagan), but rather those that exist still.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, religious or not, I can see a lot of Children of Gaia and Bone Gnawers holding Christmas in high regard, and not for any pagan origins, but rather because it represents things they hold dear, (helping the needy, giving, community, etc. . .)<br /> <br /> I imagine that the Black Furies have a very divided view on Mother's Day/Father's Day, especially as neither are too universal holidays.<br /> <br /> Personally, I tend to take the Whedon approach to Halloween. It's the night all self respecting monsters take off. Only newbs do anything on Halloween, with the exception of Wraiths, and some Mages. :P<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T10:13:06-07:00","id":726423,"title":"","content":"actually had a player who tried forcing an athiest PC On me... she.... I want to say she snuck the idea in... but she didnt think it was worth mentioning in advance... I took a &quot;shape up, or ship out&quot; attitude after a while.<br /> <br /> I decided it would be too disruptive to the game...<br /> <br /> one thing? saw a statement at least one place &quot;athiest garou do not exist<br /> <br /> <br /> somewhere else... in Dark ages though it has references to a FEW Garou Who believed themselves touched by the devil, way the flaw was phrased, it seems intended as a starting handycap to be risen above not a valid way to play the game.<br /> [<br /> and I do not disagree with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:59:55-07:00","id":726670,"title":"","content":"The problem with Shifters and Religion is that it doesn't require Faith to be religious if you have actual proof of all the beliefs and rituals actually working and being in service to something. Even the most cynical atheist will be faced with the facts that Gods are real. If he even then proceeds with saying that he doesn't want to listen to them, serve them or do what others portray as rites he has to follow he will miss out and be punished for disrespect.<br /> <br /> I think it applies similarly to anyone with other strong religious beliefs. Mind you, strong religious beliefs can be reinterpreted in the light of what the characters learn. There are some amazing Fianna, Shadow Lord and Glass Walker development spaces in using organised religion to actually spread the Gaian philosophy and outlook onto the masses.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of allowing an atheist at the beginning of a cub game... I would make it quite clear beforehand that its expected to be overcome in the first story or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:49:56-07:00","id":726776,"title":"","content":"Why? I guess depending on what exactly you mean by atheist there, it could be a problem, but a character that just doesn't buy into the idea of reincarnation, and sees the spirits maybe as aliens or some sort of scientifically explainable entity wouldn't break the game. I'm assuming it goes without saying that the person is not just trying to cause out of character issues, which is a different story. I guess it also matters if you view the WtA setting as the one true way or just a small, half false part of the greater WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:26:54-07:00","id":726874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/716811-garou-attitudes-towards-holidays?p=726776#post726776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? I guess depending on what exactly you mean by atheist there, it could be a problem, but a character that just doesn't buy into the idea of reincarnation, and sees the spirits maybe as aliens or some sort of scientifically explainable entity wouldn't break the game. I'm assuming it goes without saying that the person is not just trying to cause out of character issues, which is a different story. I guess it also matters if you view the WtA setting as the one true way or just a small, half false part of the greater WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the thread/subforum is about Garou, I am going to go out on a limb and say that their mindset is the one we are using to frame the discussion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:29:48-07:00","id":726879,"title":"","content":"Beckett, I think you're skipping a few of the books in your assessment. The IIRC the Revised players guide has a whole section on dealing with how Garou raised among modern religions deal with the world of the Garou. There are lots of examples in the books of Garou that have fused non-Garou religions with Garou culture. It's not something the books spend a lot of time on, because it isn't the focus of the game, but it isn't something ignored.<br /> <br /> The problem is that, as Cogliostro pointed out, the Garou can demonstrate the truth of much of their belief system. It's not necessarily taking the WtA setting as &quot;the one true way,&quot; but that the Garou culture and religion is based on things they don't have to take on faith. Think the Tenets of the Litany are just something some Garou made up? Well, direct servants of Gaia and Luna can be called on to confirm that these laws are things the Garou will be judged on. If you violate them, rites to acknowledge Renown and thus gain Rank (which again, have confirmation in observable effect) don't work, but rites to punish law-breakers do work.<br /> <br /> It isn't that a Garou can't have different philosophic ideas about things, but ultimately they're going to have to deal with facts other Garou can present to them, while most of the reasons to doubt the Garou religion are not things that can be easily demonstrated as fact.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T18:36:17-07:00","id":727700,"title":"","content":"It's possible, as I do not remember it being touched upon at all. Do you have any books I could check out? I have a feeling it's not what I meant, but still it would be nice to check it out, I'm less a werewolf fan as a general World of Darkness guy.<br /> <br /> As for the proof portion, I think you missed the point. A reasonable person, even by Garon standards could just as easily use their speaking with angels &lt;spirits&gt; as proof of their Faiths and debunk every Tribe Lore that the setting assumes is true just as easily as the Garon teaching their history and beliefs.<br /> <br /> The fact that they turn into a werewolf and kick demon ass that have escaped hell, wielding heavenly holy relic swords means they don't have to take it on faith, either.<br /> <br /> Don't confuse what I'm say with asserting that the WtA setting is, out of game, wrong or false within the WtA gameline. I'm talking about a character's views only, here. But, if you look at the same exact setup from a general WoD game, maybe a crossover for example, it's entirely possible the Garon are wrong.<br /> <br /> Another example, from Vampire, the Canon setting involves Cain&lt;e&gt; (and Abel), so out of game, we know for a fact that Caine, God, angels, etc. . . exist. However, not every Vampire believes that, and there are a lot of official alternative creation stories, faiths, and lore. Much of it contradicting or mutually exclusive. You can not have God make Caine the first vampire, and also Set be an actual god and the first vampire, too. But, in game, different folks believe it, and can have different degrees of proof to back it up, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 10-25-2015, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T20:38:55-07:00","id":728012,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Beckett;n727700<br /> Another example, from Vampire, the Canon setting involves Cain&lt;e&gt; (and Abel), so out of game, we know for a fact that Caine, God, angels, etc. . . exist. However, not every Vampire believes that, and there are a lot of official alternative creation stories, faiths, and lore. Much of it contradicting or mutually exclusive. You can not have God make Caine the first vampire, and also Set be an actual god and the first vampire, too. But, in game, different folks believe it, and can have different degrees of proof to back it up, too.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <br /> Except those books where its not true! There's a whole storyline about how Saulot goes east and is &quot;WTFBBQ Vampires older than caine!:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T02:41:04-07:00","id":728213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/716811-garou-attitudes-towards-holidays?p=727700#post727700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible, as I do not remember it being touched upon at all. Do you have any books I could check out? I have a feeling it's not what I meant, but still it would be nice to check it out, I'm less a werewolf fan as a general World of Darkness guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Werewolf Storytellers Handbook (Revised) has a section on it, including a sidebar about a Fianna Galliard that has managed to mesh being a Christian minister with their faith in Gaia.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure the Black Fury books address this when talking about one of their Camps which operates as a group of Catholic nuns who try to influence the faithful to be more Gaian in their philosophy even if they never divert from Christian dogma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A reasonable person, even by Garon standards could just as easily use their speaking with angels &lt;spirits&gt; as proof of their Faiths and debunk every Tribe Lore that the setting assumes is true just as easily as the Garon teaching their history and beliefs. </div> </div> </div>The problems with this assertion are:<br /> <br /> There's no real world religion for someone to be raised under that actually teaches a metaphysical system close enough to WtA cosmology for this to work. &quot;Spirits are angels and demons,&quot; doesn't really make sense unless you completely abandon how religions with angels and demons define them. If Gaian spirits are &quot;angels&quot; and Wyrm spirits are &quot;demons,&quot; what does that make Weaver and Wyld spirits? How does a Garou being able to pick up any object and awaken the spirit reflection of it jive with the idea of angels? In what faith does almost every thing sitting around have its own personal angel inside of it that can be called forth? How does it deal with a spirit getting summoned up that says, &quot;Oh, yeah, I'm an angel, but I wasn't actually created by your idea of a supreme deity, I exist because of the collective belief that I should.&quot; which is something that can be done? Heck why, in general, would the angels consistently get annoyed that you keep calling them that, and insist that they're not angels?<br /> <br /> What's their proof that debunks the mainstream core of the Gaian spirituality/religion? At best they can just change names.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that they turn into a werewolf and kick demon ass that have escaped hell, wielding heavenly holy relic swords means they don't have to take it on faith, either. </div> </div> </div>The idea that Fetishes would make sense to someone as &quot;holy relic swords&quot; doesn't really pan out. Holy relics in Christianity aren't powered by an angel that lives in the sword that needs to be cajoled or paid for service with spiritual energy gathered by meditating on the nature of the supreme deity. There are real world faiths that have a closer idea of holy relics to Fetishes, but they don't really have the same &quot;kicking demon butt in the name of the supreme deity,&quot; angle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, if you look at the same exact setup from a general WoD game, maybe a crossover for example, it's entirely possible the Garon are wrong. </div> </div> </div>The Garou are canonically wrong about all sorts of things. However, the reality of their spirituality isn't generally one of them because it is essentially both hardwired into them, and by necessity factually true. The Garou might be off one what exactly Gaia and Luna are, and their role in the greater scheme of things, but Gaia and Luna have to be real for WtA to work; even in a crossover general WoD game. The animist spirits of WtA have to be real, as well as the Garou's ancient pacts with them. Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another example, from Vampire, the Canon setting involves Cain&lt;e&gt; (and Abel), so out of game, we know for a fact that Caine, God, angels, etc. . . exist. </div> </div> </div>Except we don't. The canon setting says that European vampires (and many vampires that have fallen under the control of them) believe this. OOC we know that this is not a set in stone fact. We know there has to be a first vampire for the kindred. But as you note, there are lots of OOC canon contradictory myths about how that all went down. Nothing necessitates that an Abrahamic supreme deity (and all the other trappings such as Abrahamic angels) exists in VtM, it is just a common belief that send being is responsible for vampires. There's a big difference between the canon mythical vampire creation story, and the canon on its truth. The canon on its truth is only that some first vampire that created all the others a very long time ago had to happen. Meanwhile, with WtA, Gaia is both in-character and out-of-character a canonical truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T02:47:50-07:00","id":728218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/716811-garou-attitudes-towards-holidays?p=727700#post727700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the proof portion, I think you missed the point. A reasonable person, even by Garon standards could just as easily use their speaking with angels &lt;spirits&gt; as proof of their Faiths and debunk every Tribe Lore that the setting assumes is true just as easily as the Garon teaching their history and beliefs.<br /> <br /> The fact that they turn into a werewolf and kick demon ass that have escaped hell, wielding heavenly holy relic swords means they don't have to take it on faith, either.<br /> <br /> Don't confuse what I'm say with asserting that the WtA setting is, out of game, wrong or false within the WtA gameline. I'm talking about a character's views only, here. But, if you look at the same exact setup from a general WoD game, maybe a crossover for example, it's entirely possible the Garon are wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why Werewolf doesn't play well with others. It's a setting that's either objectively right, and whose morality and cosmology define how things work in the setting or the whole thing falls apart quicker then a house of cards. The whole game lies on the concept of their religion being the absolute truth and the core conflict of the setting stems from it being The Truth. If you want to crossover Werewolf with other games, you will either trample their cosmologies or ignore the Werewolf cosmology completely and hope your players don't try to engage with any major spiritual elements of the game.<br /> <br /> The thing you are missing is that there are Angels and Demons in Werewolf. They are distinctly not the Spirits the Garou deal with. A Garou who believes the spirit of Fenris The Wolf is actually Saint George the Dragonslayer is going to be a deeply disturbed outlier. One who is quite likely to be considered utterly insane by anyone else.<br /> <br /> Garou who do combine traditional religion apply the logic the other way around - they take their animist spirits and present them to others as God(s), angels or devils to get popular support among the traditionally faithful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T07:43:36-07:00","id":728854,"title":"","content":"Im using angels and demons as a generic catch all sense for simplicity, but not only talking about Christianity. I could see, again just an example, a Garou Hindu that holds their faith as true, finds proof of it by interpretting spirits, femori, etc. . . differently than the traditional Garou, and just feeling they are wrong.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean they are, but to the character, they might have plenty of explanations that debunk or show the normal WtA cosmology differently. They have the same onfo, just interpret it differently. I'm also saying, in my opinion, this sort of thing should be more common than I feel it is in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T08:13:53-07:00","id":728956,"title":"","content":"I just used angels and demons and St George as examples. Feel free to exchange for Aesir and Jotunn and Thor, Pandava and Rakshasa and Arjuna or any other appropriate combination.<br /> <br /> I think you really need to read up on how Werewolf actually works and what its cosmology entails before you continue this line of reasoning. Both Heavy Arms and I actually explained to you why it doesn't work like that. If you want to have a singular madman who no one in the setting takes seriously, knock yourself out, but it's not how Werewolf works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T10:47:07-07:00","id":729289,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting thread, to be sure. I think it may have strayed from the OP's original question, which I think was &quot;What are the Garou's attitude towards holidays?&quot; to the question of &quot;What are the Garou's attitude towards religion in general?&quot;<br /> <br /> For the former question, I'm surprised that no one has yet pointed out the Seasonal Rites section on pp. 43-49 in the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/61473/Werewolf-Storytellers-Handbook\" target=\"_blank\">2nd Ed Werewolf Storyteller's Handbook</a>. The Garou have adapted a number of human holidays to use in their own worship of Gaia. I especially liked the section on the Bone Gnawers celebrating Superbowl Sunday.<br /> <br /> As for the latter question, that's probably <i>alot </i>more complicated. I do remember reading about a Black Fury NPC who basically combined her Christian upbringing with her Gaia worship after her First Change. I also seem to recall that Garret Faithful, the leader of the Children of Gaia in the Amazon War also did something similar, as he likes to think of himself and his followers as following the ideals of Arthurian knights. So the attitude of the Garou towards human religions is...complex, to say the least. But one thing one has to remember is that <i>every </i>Garou can feel the pain of Gaian his heart. The Garou <i>know </i>that Gaia is real because of this. Such a thing is definitely going to color an individual Garou's attitude toward human religions in one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T12:46:40-07:00","id":729684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/716811-garou-attitudes-towards-holidays?p=728218#post728218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this is why Werewolf doesn't play well with others. It's a setting that's either objectively right, and whose morality and cosmology define how things work in the setting or the whole thing falls apart quicker then a house of cards. The whole game lies on the concept of their religion being the absolute truth and the core conflict of the setting stems from it being The Truth. If you want to crossover Werewolf with other games, you will either trample their cosmologies or ignore the Werewolf cosmology completely and hope your players don't try to engage with any major spiritual elements of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a religion. It's a definite connection to an otherworldly realm lost to the rest of the material world. It's no more a religion than the underlying structure and assumptions of, say, Changeling. Reverence itself does not constitute a religion, and while some elements of the Garou Nation can be similar to those in religious institutions, it is, on the whole and through day to day operations, way more matter of fact about everything, because spirits are right there, over their shoulders, making deals for very real and often very concrete forms of chiminage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing you are missing is that there are Angels and Demons in Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>Pending ST approval, usually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T14:14:34-07:00","id":729861,"title":"","content":"I remember reading somewhere about some Red Talons having their own &quot;parodies&quot; of human holidays like decorating trees with human organs for Christmas. I just don't remember where I found it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T17:15:53-07:00","id":730462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/716811-garou-attitudes-towards-holidays?p=729289#post729289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting thread, to be sure. I think it may have strayed from the OP's original question, which I think was &quot;What are the Garou's attitude towards holidays?&quot; to the question of &quot;What are the Garou's attitude towards religion in general?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in my defense, I was trying to use religion in general to expand more on the discussion of holidays.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/716811-garou-attitudes-towards-holidays?p=728956#post728956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you really need to read up on how Werewolf actually works and what its cosmology entails before you continue this line of reasoning. Both Heavy Arms and I actually explained to you why it doesn't work like that. If you want to have a singular madman who no one in the setting takes seriously, knock yourself out, but it's not how Werewolf works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not uneducated on how Werewolf actually works, I'm disagreeing with you. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T17:51:03-07:00","id":730530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/716811-garou-attitudes-towards-holidays?p=729861#post729861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading somewhere about some Red Talons having their own &amp;quot;parodies&amp;quot; of human holidays like decorating trees with human organs for Christmas. I just don't remember where I found it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't put it past them to do it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T19:39:51-07:00","id":730840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/716811-garou-attitudes-towards-holidays?p=729861#post729861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading somewhere about some Red Talons having their own &amp;quot;parodies&amp;quot; of human holidays like decorating trees with human organs for Christmas. I just don't remember where I found it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was in the first tribe book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T19:48:34-07:00","id":730873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/716811-garou-attitudes-towards-holidays?p=729861#post729861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading somewhere about some Red Talons having their own &quot;parodies&quot; of human holidays like decorating trees with human organs for Christmas. I just don't remember where I found it.</div> </div> </div> </div>2nd edition and Revised corebooks, in the tribal rites section, though in later Revised, this sort of edgemastering got moved to a specific camp (The Dying Cubs), who covertly use torture to strengthen caerns, and may or may not be up to no good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-26-2015, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T09:56:54-07:00","id":744641,"title":"","content":"I think people in general will care about the holidays they liked and celebrated as young. So if you're playing a &quot;humanraised&quot; garou, you will have a soft spot and a desire to celebrate the holidays you're used to. Yes, the garou seasonal rites are great, but for someone who hasn't been brought up with that, they'll prefer the human holidays. <br /> <br /> <br /> My current character can't wait for 4.july.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9019-maria-rodriguez","name":"Maria Rodriguez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T13:53:25-07:00","id":745021,"title":"","content":"There are real world examples of syncretization between Abrahamic and Animistic traditions they just tend to start looking different what you'd get with other versions of christianity or Islam. I imagine there are large groups of homids and kinfolk who follow an odd mix of modern religions and Animistic metaphysics, though their God might be female.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T17:37:34-07:00","id":745435,"title":"","content":"It's in the Storytellers Guide. They have a whole calender of Garou holidays. The only real world holiday that falls in place is Halloween. It's the Fianna's Sam Hain festivities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T06:16:16-08:00","id":749016,"title":"","content":"The 1st edition storyteller's handbook has one yearly holiday per tribe, but there are obviously more rites that are seasonal. They are often based on moon calendars, comprehensively explained in Rage across the Heavens, and therefore the dates aren't fixed towards our western calenders, but vary a little, just like easter and dated derivated from easter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:41:07-08:00","id":754610,"title":"","content":"oh any thoughts didnt notice a response to the gift &quot;Bury the wolf&quot; Being used for a holiday (Even if it isnt a calendar holiday) with ones kinfolk?<br /> <br /> or to do some horsbeack riding or whatever...<br /> <br /> e.g. think that would be a valid use for it, or that with the danger a garou puts himself in with it... not knowing when it ends and such, make it not worthwhile...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}